      ":question/problem": "Given that\n$X=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 8 & 10 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{12}=0?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 8 & 10 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3}.\n$$",
